\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces End-to-end pipeline. Raw ERP transaction feeds are cleaned into a canonical accounts/transactions schema, assembled into a temporal shadow graph, and passed through the streaming topology engine under the read-then-insert invariant, so that a feature is provably a function only of transactions strictly earlier in processing order. The resulting feature table (ordinary + topology, with offline-only TGN embeddings added for the research configuration) feeds a gradient-boosted model; the console layer attaches a TreeSHAP explanation and a re-derived evidence path to every alert. The production/online bundle omits the TGN component, since its learned memory tensor is not persisted for live inference.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{1}{2}{End-to-end pipeline. Raw ERP transaction feeds are cleaned into a canonical accounts/transactions schema, assembled into a temporal shadow graph, and passed through the streaming topology engine under the read-then-insert invariant, so that a feature is provably a function only of transactions strictly earlier in processing order. The resulting feature table (ordinary + topology, with offline-only TGN embeddings added for the research configuration) feeds a gradient-boosted model; the console layer attaches a TreeSHAP explanation and a re-derived evidence path to every alert. The production/online bundle omits the TGN component, since its learned memory tensor is not persisted for live inference}{figure.caption.1}{}}
